# Deploy to Cloudflare Workers

Until the user says to stop, publish every completed site change to the Worker `hiweb-marketing-ui`.

From the repo root, in PowerShell:

```
npx astro build; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }; npx wrangler deploy --keep-vars
```

- Always pass `--keep-vars` so existing Worker secrets stay in place.
- Staging is a separate Worker, `hiweb-marketing-ui-staging`, at https://hiweb-marketing-ui-staging.hiwebapps.workers.dev. It is SSR, password-protected, and reads Sanity drafts. Deploy it only when the staging code changes:

```
$env:PUBLIC_SITE_ENV='staging'; $env:PUBLIC_SITE_URL='https://hiweb-marketing-ui-staging.hiwebapps.workers.dev'; $env:CLOUDFLARE_ENV='staging'; npx astro build; if ($LASTEXITCODE -ne 0) { exit $LASTEXITCODE }; npx wrangler deploy --env staging --keep-vars
```

`CLOUDFLARE_ENV=staging` has to be set during the Astro build. The Cloudflare adapter writes `dist/server/wrangler.json` for the active environment, and `wrangler deploy --env staging` only matches that file. Without it, the staging bundle is published to the live Worker.

- Do not run the live build, the staging build, and `npx sanity deploy` at the same time. All three write `dist/`.
- Do not deploy Studio unless the change is a Sanity schema the editors need.
- Do not commit or push unless the user asks.
- After deploy, confirm the affected public URL returns the new markup. The site is https://hiweb-marketing-ui.hiwebapps.workers.dev
- If the browser still shows the previous version, tell the user to reload with Ctrl+F5.
